al behavior**\r\nWhen debugging into TestResourceManager I noticed that Test Resources are gathered in a TreeSet.\r\n`Set<QuarkusTestResourceLifecycleManager> testResourceRunners = new TreeSet(new QuarkusTestResourceLifecycleManagerComparator());`\r\nSo two Test Resources with the same order are considered equal and one replaces the other.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\r\n1. Implement a QuarkusTestResourceLifecycleManager with default order.\r\n2. Run tests for quarkus-amazon-lambda.\r\n\r\n**Environment (please complete the following information):**\r\n - Output of `uname -a` or `ver`: Linux sku-ubuntu 5.0.0-23-generic #24~18.04.1-Ubuntu SMP Mon Jul 29 16:12:28 UTC 2019 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux\r\n - Output of `java -version`: openjdk version \"1.8.0_222\"\r\nOpenJDK Runtime Environment (build 1.8.0_222-20190711120915.buildslave.jdk8u-src-tar--b08)\r\nOpenJDK 64-Bit GraalVM CE 19.1.1 (build 25.222-b08-jvmci-19.1-b01, mixed mode)\r\n - GraalVM version (if different from Java): \r\n - Quarkus version or git rev: 0.20.0\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nIntroduced with #3206.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"gsmet","id":1279749,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzk3NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1279749?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet","html_url":"https://github.com/gsmet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gsmet/received_events","type":"User","user_v